Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area. It is not a listed building and is not covered by a tree preservation order.

Our guidance says that replacement windows in a conservation area need a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material or the glazing pattern, for example switching from timber to uPVC or changing the glazing bar layout, you will likely need to apply. If the replacements are an exact match, you may not need one, but I can't give a formal view on that. It's worth contacting the planning desk before you order anything to confirm.

If you already have an application reference for this property, send it to me and I can look up its status.
